            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0138" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7661/9.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-09-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson states that a shipment of 100 cases of Underwood’s deviled ham,
                    Agricultural Department certificate No. 59859, has been <pb facs="0139" n="27"
                        xml:id="pg27"/> refused entry, the government analysis showing boric acid.
                    Says that he has been informed that other shipments which have already arrived
                    will be refused for the same cause.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
